cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Latin Patristic Texts: the open corpus of Bibliothecarius Modernus"
message: "If you use a text from this corpus, cite the work, the Bibliothecarius Modernus edition year and its catalog id (plNNN-SSS, see Patrologia_Latina/CATALOG_INDEX.csv), and the edition URL or DOI where one exists. Everything Bibliothecarius Modernus created here is dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0); the Latin sources are public domain."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Wolfslayer
    given-names: Ryan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8914-9706"
    affiliation: Bibliothecarius Modernus (independent project)
repository-code: "https://github.com/wryan14/Latin-Patristic-Texts"
url: "https://bibliothecarius-modernus.github.io"
abstract: >-
  The open text corpus of Bibliothecarius Modernus, an independent digital
  library of neglected Latin literature: for each published edition, the
  public-domain Latin source as used (J.-P. Migne, Patrologia Latina, or a
  named manuscript), the complete English translation, and the edition's
  translation.json with method, provenance, review status and rights.
  Editions since September 2026 carry per-segment model provenance and
  recorded corrections and passed a deterministic source-coverage check and
  an independent second-model review; earlier editions (2024-25) were made
  with lighter checks and are preserved as published, with known defects
  recorded in the library's machine-readable catalog.
keywords:
  - Latin literature
  - patristics
  - medieval theology
  - Patrologia Latina
  - translation
  - digital library
  - open access
  - CC0
license: CC0-1.0
